    "panels": [
        {
            "title": "About this dashboard",
            "type": "text",
            "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
            "options": {
                "mode": "markdown",
                "content": "This dashboard reads from **Prometheus**, fed by two different collectors:\n\n- `prometheus` (`Beberlei\\Metrics\\Collector\\Prometheus`) is scraped from the app's `/prometheus` endpoint every 15s (see `infrastructure/docker/services/prometheus/prometheus.yml`), configured with namespace `app`, so `homepage.visits` becomes the series `app_homepage_visits`. `measure()`/`timing()` set a **gauge**, `increment()`/`decrement()` change a **counter**, `gauge()` sets a gauge directly.\n- `otel` (`Beberlei\\Metrics\\Collector\\OpenTelemetry`) *pushes* OTLP straight to Prometheus's own OTLP receiver (`--web.enable-otlp-receiver`, see docker-compose.yml) instead of being scraped. Its metrics keep their raw name (no `app_` prefix) and carry a `job=\"beberlei-metrics-demo\"` label instead."
            }
        },
        {
            "title": "app_homepage_visits (counter)",
            "type": "timeseries",
            "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 4 },
            "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prom-metrics" },
            "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short" }, "overrides": [] },
            "options": {
                "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom" },
                "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" }
            },
            "targets": [
                {
                    "refId": "A",
                    "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prom-metrics" },
                    "expr": "app_homepage_visits",
                    "legendFormat": "visits"
                }
            ]
        },
